) Lung tissue in cases of congenital pulmonary lymphangiectasia with dilated lymphatic channels without lymphatic proliferation. Inset: CD31 immunohistochemical stain in a case of congenital pulmonary lymphangiectasia highlighting dilated lymphatic spaces. The positive CD31 stain in the endothelial lining confirms that the dilated spaces are lymphatic in origin, not artifacts.

